  "script": "One goat, zero enclosures? This is Gary. A nonprofit in Rosepine, Louisiana bought him so kids could practice goat roping. Gary had other plans. First he broke out of the horse pen. Then a stall. Then a kennel — reinforced, extra latches, didn't matter. Every fix, Gary found the gap. So he did the only logical thing: he moved to the shoulder of U.S. Highway 171 and just... stayed. Drivers started spotting him daily. Now he's basically DeRidder's unofficial mascot, a goat nobody owns anymore because nobody can catch him. The foundation still checks on him. He still won't come home. So who's actually in charge here — the humans, or the goat?",
